# Git push (proxy bypass)

Corporate `http.proxy` points at `gitlab.dm.korusconsulting.ru` and breaks direct `git push` to GitHub.

## Required

- **Always** push via [`scripts/git-push.ps1`](../../scripts/git-push.ps1) — never raw `git push`.
- Default (current branch → `origin`): `.\scripts\git-push.ps1`
- Explicit branch: `.\scripts\git-push.ps1 -u origin main`
- Extra git args pass through: `.\scripts\git-push.ps1 origin main --force-with-lease` (only if user orders)

## Forbidden

- `git push` / `gh` push without clearing proxy
- `git -c http.proxy= push` ad hoc — use the script (single entry point)

Script runs: `git -c http.proxy= -c https.proxy= push …` from repo root.
